      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — clearer structure (Arrange/Act/Assert), named expected-output variables, an explanatory comment on the HTML, and removal of the dead `assertContents` helper.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made for better understandability:\n\n1. **Named expected-output variables** (`fullDocumentNodes`, `div2SubtreeNodes`) so the semicolon-delimited strings have context instead of appearing as magic values.\n2. **Arrange/Act/Assert comments** clearly separate the three phases of the test.\n3. **`@DisplayName`** gives the test a human-readable description of the scenario being verified.\n4. **Javadoc on helpers** (`assertIterates`, `trackSeen`) explain their contracts so readers don't have to infer them.\n5. **Removed dead code** — the unused `assertContents` helper was deleted since it was never called and only added noise.\n6. **Inline comment on the HTML fixture** shows the structure at a glance without having to mentally parse the HTML string."
